Below are a few of the primary responsibilities your internship would include, more detail will be provided when we meet:
Provide administrative support to the Leasing Team including reports, lease documentation, preparation of offers to lease and all other documentation as required;
Accompany Leasing Managers on property tours.
Update Broker contacts in contacts database;
Order floor plans through space plan provider;
Organize and distribute information (floor plans, marketing materials) to brokers and tenants as required;
Prepare accurate & timely internal reporting, as required;
Field calls on general leasing inquiries from industry contacts, as required;
Maintain vacancy listings on our website and update monthly availability report and/or other data management functions;
Assist in the coordination, production, and distribution of all leasing marketing materials and initiatives including broker and tenant functions, brochures, and all other marketing materials as required;
Code, process and file all expenses related to Leasing Business Unit;
Work with other internal departments (Property Management, Construction, Finance & Accounting, Acquisitions, etc.) as required on related issues;
What skills and experience do you require?
Here's what we need you to bring to the table:
Creative mindset and ability to think outside the box.
Passionate about Real Estate.
Flexible, well-organized, able to work well under pressure and tight deadlines in a fast-paced, high volume, team environment.
Proficient in a variety of software programs (including Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook and Adobe Acrobat).
The most important attributes we are looking for: enthusiasm, the ability to have fun while working hard, sincerity and a willingness to learn and grow.
Who are we?
Dream is a leading developer of exceptional office and residential assets in Toronto, owns stabilized income-generating assets in both Canada and the U.S., and has a successful asset management business with $28 billion of assets under management. We also develop land and residential assets in Western Canada. Our entrepreneurial spirit drives us to seize unconventional opportunities and approach every project with passion and purpose. At Dream, we care about our employees, provide exciting work opportunities, open work environments, and fun events, fostering an atmosphere where continuous learning and innovation thrive. Join us and make a difference.
Due to the high volume of applications, only candidates who qualify will be contacted. Interviews will be conducted in an assessment centre-style on a pre-arranged date in October 2025.
Dream Unlimited is committed to workplace diversity and provides accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout our hiring process. If you require accommodation through any aspect of our process, please let us know and we will work with you to meet your needs.

